            ":encompassing/rationale": "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account linear: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: linear=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/linear-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1856->3029. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json.",
            ":encompassing/topic": {
